        81.83369445800781
      ],
      "text": "It is critical to ensure proper follow-up and evaluation for TB and other diseases in household contacts",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.973668098449707,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        80.59070587158203,
        527.4567260742188,
        95.03370666503906
      ],
      "text": "with abnormal CXR findings or TB symptoms. The investigations should be performed in accordance",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.999650001525879,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        93.79071807861328,
        527.3992309570312,
        108.23371887207031
      ],
      "text": "with national guidelines and sound clinical practice. Contacts found not to have TB disease should",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        106.99073028564453,
        527.382568359375,
        121.43373107910156
      ],
      "text": "be assessed for TPT. Although TBI testing is not a requirement for initiating TPT, it may be done as a",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        120.19074249267578,
        284.21661376953125,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "part of eligibility screening where feasible (see",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        284.2167053222656,
        120.19074249267578,
        333.2877197265625,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": "section 1.3",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        333.2923889160156,
        120.19074249267578,
        341.8503723144531,
        134.6337432861328
      ],
      "text": ").",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        141.8946075439453,
        527.5987548828125,
        156.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "A previous history of TB or TPT should not be a contraindication for TPT in cases of re-exposure, after",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.984689712524414,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        155.09474182128906,
        527.4178466796875,
        169.53773498535156
      ],
      "text": "exclusion of reactivated disease. Such individuals, including those with fibrotic radiological lesions,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        167.01869201660156,
        527.4091186523438,
        182.7377471923828
      ],
      "text": "(65,66) . The choice of TPT also depends on the presence  may be at increased risk of progression",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        181.4947052001953,
        527.4246826171875,
        195.9376983642578
      ],
      "text": "of contraindications (e.g. active hepatitis or symptoms of peripheral neuropathy when isoniazid is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        194.69471740722656,
        527.5593872070312,
        209.13771057128906
      ],
      "text": "considered) or the likelihood of drug–drug interactions, particularly when rifamycin regimes are being",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.977426528930664,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        207.8946075439453,
        145.6804962158203,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "considered (see",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        145.6800994873047,
        207.8946075439453,
        194.7510986328125,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": "section 1.4",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        194.75579833984375,
        207.8946075439453,
        200.2998046875,
        222.3376007080078
      ],
      "text": ").",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8662109375,
        229.5985870361328,
        527.6337890625,
        244.0415802001953
      ],
      "text": "Different symptom screening approaches have different sensitivity and specificity. The facility of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8662109375,
        242.79859924316406,
        527.5675659179688,
        257.2416076660156
      ],
      "text": "symptom screening makes it a much more accessible programme option. Symptom screening is",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8662109375,
        255.9987335205078,
        527.333251953125,
        270.4417419433594
      ],
      "text": "standard in a clinical workup and can be repeated as often as necessary. In contrast, additional",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8662109375,
        269.1986083984375,
        527.428955078125,
        283.6416320800781
      ],
      "text": "resources are necessary for CXR and mWRDs. Scaling up mWRDs for diagnosis should be prioritized",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.8662109375,
        282.39862060546875,
        527.4402465820312,
        296.8416442871094
      ],
      "text": "(if full access has not yet been achieved) before scaling it up for screening, as it requires significant",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        295.5986328125,
        524.42236328125,
        310.0416564941406
      ],
      "text": "resources, including increased capacity in and expansion of diagnostic and sample transport networks.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.964391708374023,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        317.302490234375,
        527.564453125,
        331.7455139160156
      ],
      "text": "Countries should include the W4SS, CRP, CXR and mWRD in national TB screening algorithms",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        330.5025939941406,
        527.374755859375,
        344.94561767578125
      ],
      "text": "according to their feasibility, the level of the health facility, resources and equity. While all four tools",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        343.7024841308594,
        527.4468383789062,
        358.1455078125
      ],
      "text": "are recommended for people with HIV, CRP is particularly accurate for TB screening of people who",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        356.9026184082031,
        527.409912109375,
        371.34564208984375
      ],
      "text": "are not yet receiving ART, and CXR enhances the sensitivity of the W4SS in people receiving ART, both",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.980082511901855,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        370.10260009765625,
        527.4058227539062,
        384.5456237792969
      ],
      "text": "of which might be considered when choosing algorithms. Consideration should also be given to the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        383.3025207519531,
        524.4114379882812,
        397.74554443359375
      ],
      "text": "added benefit of including CRP for ruling out TB disease before initiating TPT among people with HIV.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.983838081359863,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        405.0065002441406,
        527.5648803710938,
        419.44952392578125
      ],
      "text": "CXR has been used to screen for TB for several decades. CXRs are also routinely used to triage people",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.976725578308105,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        418.2065124511719,
        527.2088012695312,
        432.6495361328125
      ],
      "text": "presenting for care who show signs, symptoms or risk factors for TB to determine the most appropriate",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.955108642578125,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        431.406494140625,
        527.4107055664062,
        445.8495178222656
      ],
      "text": "clinical pathway for proper evaluation. In many settings, however, use of CXR for TB screening and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        444.60650634765625,
        527.4322509765625,
        459.0495300292969
      ],
      "text": "triage for TB disease is limited by the paucity of health personnel trained to interpret radiographic",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        457.8065185546875,
        527.4356689453125,
        472.2495422363281
      ],
      "text": "images and by substantial intra- and inter-reader variation in its accuracy to detect abnormalities",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        469.7304992675781,
        324.1138000488281,
        485.4495544433594
      ],
      "text": "(13) . CAD is useful in such situations. associated with TB",
